      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2x-3)^2&=x^2+(x-2)^2-2x(x-2)\\cos120^{\\circ}\\\\4x^2-12x+9&=3x^2-6x+4\\\\x^2-6x+5&=0\\\\(x-1)(x-5)&=0\\\\x&=1\\text{ or }5\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x=1$, $AC=x-2=-1$, so this root is inadmissible. For $x=5$, the side lengths are $3$, $5$ and $7$, all positive.\nHence, $x=5$.",
